      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, you still need medical attention immediately because a stroke can resolve quickly (transient ischemic attack) and only a medical scan can rule out a life-threatening emergency. Migraines do not typically cause rapid onset speech or facial drooping that persists, even briefly, without a more severe underlying cause. Please go to the ER now and tell the doctors you had sudden weakness or slurring that appeared minutes ago, as this is the critical time for diagnosis.",
